# Match game-is-up: keep build context small and reproducible. Secrets are excluded by the
# block at the end of this file.
node_modules
**/node_modules
# Nested task worktrees (user-level rule: .worktrees/<name>/) are separate checkouts.
.worktrees
**/dist
# The incremental state must go wherever dist goes. Excluding the OUTPUT while shipping tsc's record
# that it was already produced makes the in-image build a silent no-op: `tsc` reads .tsbuildinfo,
# concludes everything is emitted, writes nothing, and the next workspace fails to resolve the types
# it was supposed to emit ("Cannot find module '@printstream/shared'"). Only reproduces for someone
# who has built locally, so CI's fresh checkout never sees it.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite
**/.cache
.git
.github
.vscode
**/coverage
data
!data/demo-library
!data/demo-library/**
!data/demo-camera-snapshots
!data/demo-camera-snapshots/**
!data/demo-captures
!data/demo-captures/**
apps/api/data
apps/bridge/release
.artifacts
!apps/web/src/data
!apps/web/src/data/**
apps/web/public/README.md
deploy
*.log
tmp

# Secrets, at every depth (SEC-7), last so no exception above can re-include one. Docker matches a
# bare `.env` only at the context root, so a nested env file, dev certificate or key would otherwise
# be copied into the image. Env templates stay (db:generate uses a placeholder, not a real .env).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env*.example
**/.secrets
**/.aws
**/*.pfx
**/*.cer
**/*.der
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
.windows-build
.backups
